# command: python3 -u /tmp/tag_leak_probe.py ; python3 -u /tmp/tag_leak_probe2.py   (board, root, /dev/mem)
# bitstream: 529594D7B365317D07339B5EDB202A3F   boot.bin: 06f264a7… (Phase-2 image; this bitstream is JTAG-loaded)
# commit: n/a (DEV working copy, not a git checkout)
# date: 2026-10-22
#
# Probe of the DIRTY_PUSH tag rule (no epoch needed: only the dirty FIFO is used).
# Probe 1: K=3 pushes per trial, flush between trials, tight vs. with a read-back
#          (a bus barrier) after every push.
# Probe 2: K=1/2/3, and K=3 with a real 10 ms gap between pushes; state read
#          immediately and again 50 ms later.
# Result: the write path redelivers a store twice and the copies are NOT always
# adjacent, so one logical push can enqueue two records of the same id --
# independent of pacing.  See README (Phase 3A/3B) and AGENTS.md #18.

